          "Legacy SMS and push notification MFA are vulnerable to SIM swapping and adversary-in-the-middle (AiTM) phishing proxies (like Evilginx). The gold standard today is **FIDO2 / WebAuthn**, which cryptographically binds authentication credentials to the specific browser domain origin using public-key cryptography, making phishing mathematically impossible.",
